+HIS-16 (#237) — vacuity checks
+==============================
+
+Produced by scratchpad/his16/vacuity.py, reproduced in full at the bottom.
+Every mutation is applied to a COMMITTED tree and reverted from a byte copy
+taken by the harness — never `git checkout --`, which restores to HEAD and has
+eaten an agent's uncommitted work twice in this epic (DEF-035).
+
+The three mechanisms from results/epic-home-integrity-sync/validation/
+vacuity-ledger.md, and how each is answered:
+
+  A  the probe reddens a PRECONDITION, not the claim
+     -> every row names the assertion(s) that actually reddened, and the
+        verdict line says whether that set is exactly the claim. A row that is
+        not exactly the claim is printed as MISMATCH and kept.
+
+  B  the FIXTURE cannot express the defect
+     -> ConfinementTest's refusal case asserts its own precondition first and
+        is blind to the mutation under test: it reads Confinement.covers,
+        which V1 does not touch.
+     -> the membership law's self-test plants DEF-047's exact residue — a unit
+        gone with ONLY its .projections.json surviving — AND, since review of
+        #241, a .projections.json beside every LIVE unit. The second half was
+        missing, and its absence is what made V4a's first diagnosis wrong.
+
+  C  the mutation never REACHED the code
+     -> the harness asserts `s.count(old) == 1` before every mutation.
+
+RUNNER: `jbang RunHis16.java` (ConfinementTest), plus the membership law run
+standalone with --result-out.
+
+WHY JsonContractTest IS NOT IN THE MUTATION LANE
+------------------------------------------------
+It drives `project register|remove|resolve|sync` on their REAL execution
+paths, which is safe only because the confinement guard refuses them. Run that
+suite with the guard mutated away and it does not go red: it REPRODUCES
+DEF-047 against whatever checkout the JVM is standing in. Its dependence on
+the guard is measured the other way round — asserted GREEN on the unmutated
+tree, where all four entries reach the refusal and get exit 14 with one JSON
+document carrying the typed code.
+
+The end-to-end escape IS reproduced under control by the graph node
+home-integrity/ProjectVerbStaysInItsHome, which owns a throwaway victim.
+
+CORRECTIONS AFTER REVIEW OF #241
+--------------------------------
+M3  V4a's DIAGNOSIS was wrong, and the reason is this ledger's own mechanism
+    B. The law lane runs with ZERO real homes, so the only .projections.json
+    in scope was the orphan the "lost" fixture plants — the single file for
+    which reading it under the mangled name still lands in the right bucket. A
+    real home has one beside every LIVE unit, and under V4a's mutation each
+    becomes a spurious LOST. It was never benign redundancy: it is a MASS
+    FALSE POSITIVE that would have reddened the claim on all five homes of
+    home-integrity. Mechanism B, occurring inside the instrument built to
+    count mechanism B. plant() now writes a .projections.json beside every
+    live unit; V4a re-measured below now reddens, and its self-test line shows
+    the false positive directly — "consistent home -> 2 violation(s)", a home
+    whose three readers agree being flagged.
+
+M4  V5's prose quoted an assertion that PASSES. The claim that carries "zero
+    homes fails" is at_least_one_home_was_actually_checked. Mechanism C,
+    inside the probe demonstrating mechanism C.
+
+RESULTS
+-------
+BASELINE
+    RunHis16: 8 cases, all PASS
+    membership law self-test: passed
+
+V1  the CWD/confinement check in ProjectRoot removed
+    mutation: ProjectRoot.resolve: `if (!confinement.covers(root))` -> `if (false)`
+    expected to redden: ['a confined process refuses a CWD-derived root outside the root', 'an explicit --project-dir OUTSIDE the root is refused too']
+    ACTUALLY reddened:  ['a confined process refuses a CWD-derived root outside the root', 'an explicit --project-dir OUTSIDE the root is refused too']
+    verdict: the claim reddened, and only the claim
+
+V2  the working-directory axis dropped from Confinement.current()
+    mutation: Confinement.current: the `axes.add(axis(CWD, ...))` line deleted
+    expected to redden: ['every axis is read, and the working directory is one of them']
+    ACTUALLY reddened:  ['every axis is read, and the working directory is one of them']
+    verdict: the claim reddened, and only the claim
+    This is the scope-2 claim itself: a sandbox report that does not cover CWD is the pre-#237 state, where five variables were pinned and the sixth axis was never asked about.
+
+V3  an UNSET axis treated as confined rather than as an escape
+    mutation: Confinement.axis: a null value now reads as inside
+    expected to redden: ['an UNSET agent variable is an escape, not a pass']
+    ACTUALLY reddened:  ['an UNSET agent variable is an escape, not a pass']
+    verdict: the claim reddened, and only the claim
+    SmEnv's class comment records what an unset agent root costs: five units projected into three real agent homes.
+
+V4a  the .projections.json BRANCH disabled (first attempt)
+    mutation: HomeMembershipLaw.installedRecords: `if (n.endsWith(...))` -> `if (false)`
+    expected to redden: ['the_detector_flags_a_planted_gain_and_a_planted_loss']
+    ACTUALLY reddened:  ['the_detector_flags_a_planted_gain_and_a_planted_loss']
+    verdict: the claim reddened, and only the claim
+    Re-measured after M3 fixed the fixture. What this mutation really does to a REAL home is turn every live unit's .projections.json into a spurious LOST; the fixtures could not show that until plant() started writing one beside each live unit.
